{"name":"Caribbean Sea","hex":"#0087a7","fetched":"2026-10-12","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"Caribbean Sea","whole":true,"parts":[{"part":"Proper noun","definitions":["A tropical sea in the Western Hemisphere, part of the Atlantic Ocean, southeast of the Gulf of Mexico."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/Caribbean_Sea"}],"entries":[{"title":"Caribbean Sea","blocks":[{"text":"The Caribbean Sea is a sea of the North Atlantic Ocean in the tropics of the Western Hemisphere, located south of the Gulf of Mexico and southwest of the Sargasso Sea. It is bounded by the Greater Antilles to the north from Cuba to Puerto Rico, the Lesser Antilles to the east from the Virgin Islands to Trinidad and Tobago, South America to the south from the Venezuelan coastline to the Colombian coastline, and Central America and the Yucatán Peninsula to the west from Panama to Mexico. The geopolitical region around the Caribbean Sea, including the numerous islands of the West Indies and adjacent coastal areas in the mainland of the Americas, is known as the Caribbean."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/4/44/Karibik_NASA_World_Wind_Globe.jpg/330px-Karibik_NASA_World_Wind_Globe.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Caribbean_Sea","wikidata":"Q1247"},{"title":"Caribbean","blocks":[{"text":"The Caribbean is a geo-political region in the middle of the Americas centered around the Caribbean Sea in the North Atlantic Ocean, mostly overlapping with the West Indies. Bordered by North America to the north and also the west through Central America, and South America to the south, it comprises numerous islands, cays, islets, reefs, and banks."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/4/4b/Central_America_and_the_Caribbean_Shaded_Relief_Map.png/330px-Central_America_and_the_Caribbean_Shaded_Relief_Map.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Caribbean","wikidata":"Q664609"},{"title":"Sea","blocks":[{"text":"A sea is a very large body of salty water. The term has two distinct meanings. The first is the interconnected body of seawater that spans most of Earth, known as the sea or the ocean. The second is a named body of water: usually either a marginal sea, or a large, nearly landlocked body of water."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/1/1c/Mediterranean_Sea_16.61811E_38.99124N.jpg/330px-Mediterranean_Sea_16.61811E_38.99124N.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Sea","wikidata":"Q165"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/c/c2/Tulum-Seaside-2010.jpg/500px-Tulum-Seaside-2010.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/c/c2/Tulum-Seaside-2010.jpg/1280px-Tulum-Seaside-2010.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/c/c2/Tulum-Seaside-2010.jpg/500px-Tulum-Seaside-2010.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Tulum, a Mayan city on the coast of the Caribbean in the state of Quintana Roo, Mexico","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3ATulum-Seaside-2010.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/4/49/Caribbean_plate_tectonics-en.png/500px-Caribbean_plate_tectonics-en.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/4/49/Caribbean_plate_tectonics-en.png/500px-Caribbean_plate_tectonics-en.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Caribbean plate tectonics","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3ACaribbean_plate_tectonics-en.png"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia